WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:07.300
In general, humans primarily function off
of self-interest.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:13.650
This sounds like a sad thought to bear that
even in the purist appearing of people, self-interest

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.910
can still remain.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:20.110
But perhaps it’s not entirely a bad thing.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:25.869
Perhaps we can use selfishness to achieve
selfLESSness.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:31.500
On commercial airplanes, in the case of an
oxygen shortage, adults are instructed to

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:39.179
put oxygen masks on themselves before they
assist children or other incapable passengers.

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:46.120
Arguably, this could be considered selfish,
but its purpose is selfLESS.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.579
It is logical.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:53.780
An individual cannot help anyone breathe if
they are unable to breathe themselves.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:00.999
Likewise, one cannot give something to the
world if they do not have it themselves.

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:07.010
An unhappy person cannot help the world be
happy and a person without love cannot give

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.320
the world love.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:15.830
In life, a person must first work to satisfy
their own needs, even if they may initially

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:18.690
appear selfish.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:26.110
Needs like survival, self-love, self-awareness,
self-fulfillment, and so on.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:32.860
If our selfish acts are calculated and purposeful
towards providing us with the capacity to

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:40.930
carry out the needs of others, we move through
selfishness and into selflessness.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:48.130
The problem with this process is how easy
it is to become swept away by our self-interest

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.560
and forget about the purpose of using it to
achieve selflessness.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:02:02.110
We are seductive to ourselves and easily become
addicted to creating a world around our ego.

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:09.459
We must resist, though, and maintain a balance
between our self and the rest of the world.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:12.730
Well-being is rooted in altruism.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.099
It cannot merely be self-oriented.

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:23.319
Just like a financial investor invests portions
of their money into a business, you must invest

00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:30.580
portions of yourself into others and trust
that your quality of life will accrue in value.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:37.900
And when it does, you will ironically end
up with what your selfishness wanted the whole

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:41.170
time; a better life.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:47.209
But at least in this case, you will have positively
affected others along the way and will have

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:52.120
shared in a collective happiness that is enduring
and wondrous.

